.docname {Trying a build}
.include {docs}

> **Temporary development section.** During the internal review, builds are published to the GitLab Package Registry of the
> `karbone` project, unsigned. Maven Central publication happens from GitHub once the review is done.

## Gradle setup

```kotlin
repositories {
    mavenCentral()
    maven {
        url = uri("https://gitlab.ekino.com/api/v4/projects/8920/packages/maven")
        name = "GitLab"
        credentials(HttpHeaderCredentials::class) {
            name = "Private-Token"                 // or "Deploy-Token"
            value = providers.gradleProperty("gitlabToken").get()
        }
        authentication { create<HttpHeaderAuthentication>("header") }
    }
}

dependencies {
    implementation("com.ekino.oss:karbone:0.1.0")   // or 0.1.0-SNAPSHOT
}
```

Put `gitlabToken=<personal access token with read_api>` in `~/.gradle/gradle.properties`. Inside a GitLab pipeline of the same group,
use `name = "Job-Token"` and `value = System.getenv("CI_JOB_TOKEN")` instead.

## What gets published

- `v*` tags publish the tagged version automatically.
- The `publish` job on `main` is manual and publishes the current `localVersion` snapshot.
- Packages: https://gitlab.ekino.com/iperia/karbone/-/packages
